Required regression scenarios

Manual attacks

* Attack 1 always requests Attack 1.
* Attack 2 always requests Attack 2.
* Attack 1 cannot automatically become Attack 2 during cooldown.
* Attack 2 cannot automatically become Attack 1 during cooldown.
* Repeated input during an active attack does not create a follow-up queue.
* Held input does not generate extra attacks.
* An explicitly pressed different attack can still cancel when the established combat rules allow it.
* An attack rejected due to cooldown or other restrictions must not improperly cancel the current attack.

Manual positioning

* Out-of-range melee attacks do not automatically approach the opponent.
* Attacks execute at the player’s current position.
* An out-of-range attack can naturally miss.
* Manual Dash and air dash remain operational.
* Dash Energy consumption remains correct.
* Character-authored moving attacks retain their original movement.
* Aerial attacks do not automatically move toward an opponent.
* Normal facing and directional input behavior are preserved.

Combos

* Attack 1 into Attack 2 remains possible through two explicit inputs.
* Attack 2 into Attack 1 remains possible through two explicit inputs.
* Valid authored combo routes, hit-cancels, and their timing rules remain functional.
* Rework basic-string tests so they use explicit Attack 1 / Attack 2 presses rather than the deleted automatic follow-up.
* Preserve meaningful combo coverage and character behavior; do not weaken assertions merely to make the suite pass.

Input devices

Run equivalent manual-input tests for:

* Keyboard
* Touch controls
* Game controller

Verify that each device generates the same intended attacks without automatic substitution.

Settings and UI

* No Combat settings tab.
* No assist options or stale accessibility elements.
* No queued-follow-up highlight.
* No assist strings in the active localization tables.
* Existing version 7 settings migrate without losing unrelated preferences.
* Older supported settings versions still migrate.
* The Settings dialog remains fully navigable.

Game modes

